# #1099 Stage 1: the WinUI RichEditBox hosted in a WPF compose-shaped window (Tools/EditorHostSpike).
# The spike opens with the To box focused. The body starts with one line of text and the caret on
# the empty second line.
w 4
# Give NVDA a focus change in this window before the test (a relaunch can leave it on the old one).
q {TAB}
w 2
q +{TAB}
w 3

# 0. The body is part of the window: Tab reaches it, by name, and the title is the window's.
k {TAB}
w 3
e Subject
k {TAB}
w 3
e Message body
n t
w 3
e Editor host spike

# 1. Typed-word echo (#300, #906): each word as Space ends it, and the last as Enter ends it.
#    "the" and "toast" are here because plain letters used to trigger the window's access keys.
t one two the toast three
w 3
e one
e two
e the
e toast
k {ENTER}
w 3
e three

# The rest of the text, typed without logging.
Q Alpha line
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
Q Beta line
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
Q Gamma
q {ENTER}
Q A much longer line of text here
q {ENTER}
Q Short
q {ENTER}
Q End
w 3

# 2. Down from the top: each line once, blank lines as blank (#891).
k ^{HOME}
w 3
e This line has a bold word
k {DOWN}
w 3
e one two the toast three
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Alpha line
k {DOWN}
w 3
e blank
e! Beta
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Beta line
k {DOWN}
w 3
e blank
e! Gamma
k {DOWN}
w 3
e blank
e! Gamma
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Gamma

# 3. From the end of a long line, Down onto a shorter one: that line alone.
k {DOWN}
w 3
e A much longer line of text here
k {END}
w 2
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Short
e! End

# 4. Ctrl+Down / Ctrl+Up by paragraph (#1077).
k ^{HOME}
w 3
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e one two the toast three
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e Alpha line
e! Gamma
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e blank
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e Beta line
e! Gamma
k ^{UP}
w 3
e blank
k ^{UP}
w 3
e Alpha line
e! Beta

# 5. Characters and words.
k {HOME}
w 2
k {RIGHT}
w 3
e l
k ^{RIGHT}
w 3
e line

# 6. Leaving and coming back: Shift+Tab, Tab, access keys, F6.
k +{TAB}
w 3
e Subject
k {TAB}
w 3
e Message body
k %t
w 3
e To
k %y
w 3
e Message body
k %u
w 3
e Subject
k {F6}
w 3
e Message body
k {F6}
w 3
e To
k +{F6}
w 3
e Message body

# 7. Commands from the body: Send (the status line), the menu, a dialog, the command palette.
k ^{ENTER}
w 4
e Send pressed
k %f
w 3
e Send
k {ESC}
w 2
k {ESC}
w 3
e Message body
k ^d
w 4
e Spike dialog
k {ENTER}
w 4
e Message body
k ^+p
w 4
e Command palette
k {ESC}
w 4
e Message body
